OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Nearly 60 people have been rescued
OL,6, after a US passenger jet crashed into
OL,7, the East River in New York.
OL,9,FThe US Air Boeing 737, flight 5050,
OL,10,Fcrashed shortly after take-off from
OL,11,FLa Guardia airport.
OL,13,FThe pilot tried to abort take-off at
OL,14,Fthe last minute, and the plane broke
OL,15,Finto three sections as it plunged into
OL,16,Fthe river.
OL,18,FTwo people are reported to have been
OL,19,Fkilled. A total of 45 people were taken
OL,20,Fto hospital; nine are said to be in a
OL,21,Fcritical condition.
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A High Court judge has ruled that a
OL,6, black child should have another chance
OL,7, with her natural mother before any
OL,8, decision on adoption can be taken.
OL,10,FMr Justice Cazalet said all parties
OL,11,Finvolved had agreed on a final effort
OL,12,Fto rehabilitate the baby with her
OL,13,F17-year-old black mother.
OL,15,FThe baby was taken from her mother
OL,16,Fearly in her life and the child's white
OL,17,Ffoster-mother asked Islington Council
OL,18,Fif she could adopt her permanently.
OL,20,FIslington Council does not allow black
OL,21,Fchildren to be adopted by white parents
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A UDR soldier accused of murdering two
OL,6, Catholics was alleged to have targeted
OL,7, them for loyalist murder squads from
OL,8, the banned Ulster Freedom Fighters.
OL,10,FThe accusation was made during a High
OL,11,FCourt bail application by 25-year-old
OL,12,FAndrew Brown, a former regular soldier
OL,13,Ffrom Scotland.
OL,15,FHe is charged with the murder of
OL,16,FLoughlin Maginn in August and barman
OL,17,FLiam McKee in June. Bail was refused.
OL,19,FA Crown lawyer said Mr Brown had
OL,20,Fgiven the names of 14 IRA suspects to
OL,21,Fa UDA paramilitary contact in Lisburn.
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Northern Ireland security minister Mr
OL,6, John Cope has denied collusion between
OL,7, the security forces and terrorists.
OL,9,FSpeaking to journalists, he dismissed
OL,10,Fallegations by SDLP deputy leader Mr
OL,11,FSeamus Mallon that there was a policy
OL,12,Fof collusion.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Mallon had implied that confidential
OL,15,Fdocuments listing IRA suspects did not
OL,16,Ffind their way into the hands of
OL,17,Floyalist paramilitaries by accident.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe security forces are investigating
OL,20,Fthe disappearance of the confidential
OL,21,Fdocuments.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Chief Constable of the RUC has said
OL,6, the force will not tolerate wrongdoing
OL,7, uncovered in its own ranks.
OL,9,FMr Hugh Annesley added that criminality
OL,10,Fwill be dealt with without fear or
OL,11,Ffavour.
OL,13,FHe said he took no pleasure in stating
OL,14,Fthat confidential documents had gone
OL,15,Fmissing, but the public had a right to
OL,16,Fknow.
OL,18,FMr Annesley was referring to missing
OL,19,Flists of IRA suspects that are said to
OL,20,Fhave found their way to loyalist
OL,21,Fextremists.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Green Party's annual conference
OL,6, opened in Wolverhampton today with a
OL,7, condemnation of the Government's
OL,8, approach to green issues.
OL,10,FThe party's international secretary, Ms
OL,11,FSara Parkin, said the Government did
OL,12,Fnot understand the scale of the
OL,13,Fecological crisis facing the earth.
OL,15,FIt preferred to steal individual Green
OL,16,Fpolicies rather than adopt the whole
OL,17,FGreen approach, she said.
OL,19,S/FThe conference congratulated the
OL,20,FEuropean Commission for deciding to
OL,21,Fprosecute Britain over its dirty water.
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
