PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789945424
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Prime Minister has met the United
OL,6, States Vice-President, Mr Dan Quayle,
OL,7, during her visit to Japan.
OL,9,FThey are both attending meetings of the
OL,10,FInternational Democratic Union in
OL,11,FTokyo. Their discussions covered East-
OL,12,FWest relations and arms control.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMrs Thatcher is due to meet President
OL,15,FGorbachev during a brief stop-over in
OL,16,FMoscow on her way home. She earlier
OL,17,Fdescribed him as "bold and visionary."
OL,18,F
OL,19,S/FJapan's trade minister told the Prime
OL,20,FMinister imports would be encouraged.
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
